			<div class="head">
								<div class="title" id="post-title-4836277">
																	<a href="/forum/t-13893382/scp-draft:the-place-i-belong#post-4836277">Re: SCP Draft: The Place I Belong</a>
									</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/quadraginta" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6391595); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6391595&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607110086" alt="Quadraginta" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6391595)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/quadraginta" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6391595); return false;" >Quadraginta</a></span> <span class="odate time_1607109439 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">04 Dec 2020 19:17</span>
																	<br/>
						in discussion <a href="/forum/c-50864/help:drafts-critique">Writing Help / Help: Drafts Critique</a> &raquo;
						<a href="/forum/t-13893382/scp-draft:the-place-i-belong">SCP Draft: The Place I Belong</a>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4836277">
									

<p>Hey, Grig! I'll take a look for ya!</p>
<p>Just know that my clinical tone is meh, but I'm a lot better with dialogue.</p>
<p>Alrighty.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+Let's&nbsp;do&nbsp;it!</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-Let's&nbsp;do&nbsp;it!</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>Disinformation campaigns are to be spearheaded to label SCP-XXXX-A as a UNESCO World Friendship and Peace Village to draw in more tourism.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The fact that a ConProc demands more attention is already weird enough to draw me in.<br />
I dig it.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-XXXX is a series of anomalous dreams that can occur in a certain segment of the population of Europe and Asia: most often creatives and individuals who attest to feeling at odds with society.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I feel personally called out here and I'm not sure how to mentally process this.</p>
<p>I just finished the <strong>Description</strong> and I don't really have any qualms with it. The dream sequences reminds me heavily of the River Styx and Charon, something I'm not sure if you did on purpose or not.<br />
Either way, no clinical issues so far.</p>
<p>Aside from this:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>genius loci</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Did you mean 'genus'?</p>
<p>A little confused on that bit. I had to Google 'loci' and it gave me stuff about genetics and mathematics, neither of which this piece seems to be going for. I&#8230;actually no clue what this bit is supposed to show.</p>
<p>I'm normally not a fan of free verse (that is what that poetry style is, right?), but the poem written by Tefvik is wonderfully done and the allusions to the hooded figure in the SCP-XXXX dreams is also nicely done.</p>
<p>Especially 'blessed be the stones of your dreaming streets.'</p>
<blockquote>
<p>prototypical oneirosensory visualization recording device.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Ironic&#8230;we're both currently drafting something that headcanons pioneering dream-recording Foundation tech.</p>
<p>I&#8230;don't know how to process this either.</p>
<p>I do think this is great headcanon, and I think your method of wording this is a lot better and a lot more developed than mine.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Dr. Rossi has confirmed that she is experiencing SCP-XXXX events and has been periodically for the previous three weeks.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>We can clean this up and shorten it into, 'Dr. Rossi has confirmed that she has been periodically experiencing SCP-XXXX events for the previous three weeks.'</p>
<blockquote>
<p>[ Initial view is of a mist shrouded body of water, which appears to be a river. The night is dark, with only a crescent moon serving as illumination.]</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Unnecessary extra space before 'Initial' and after the bracket.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>[The boat has stopped directly in front of subject in a manner inconsistent with the flowing water of the river, as if being held in place. The figure extends his arm out with an open palm.]</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I love dream logic. This is a lovely detail to show how unearthly this place is. Other than, you know, the weird hooded figure, the mist and—<br />
You know what I mean.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Sixteen minutes of footage are lost due to technical failure.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Both of our headcanoned dream-recording technology also involves significant lapses in dream recording to simulate the feeling of actual dream timeline-logic.</p>
<p>That's&#8230;frighteningly coincidental.</p>
<p>I love it. Love it, love it, love it &lt;3</p>
<blockquote>
<p>[Subject is within the village, walking down its streets. The stone buildings resemble architecture from the 18the century</p>
</blockquote>
<p>There's an extra 'e' in '18th'</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Rossi: The air is chilly, like an early spring night but not so cold as to be uncomfortable. Significant moisture in the air, consistent with misty conditions. The river in front of me is jet black, I cannot tell how deep it is by eye. I –”</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This is very prose-y instead of diaogue-y (if that makes sense), but this is a dream and we could say she is trying to ground herself in a world where normal logic doesn't function.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>[Sounds of a scuffle and Rossi cursing loudly cursing.]</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Two 'cursing's here.</p>
<p>Removing either would fix it, funny enough.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Many instances8 of SCP-XXXX-1 are seen lining the square and staring at subject.]</p>
</blockquote>
<p>There has been no mention of SCP-XXXX-1 up until this point, so I don't know what they're supposed to be.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Subject stands in a town square, the cobble stones shifting beneath her feet.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I absolutely adore the usage of dream logic and dream visuals here.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Answers don’t come in dreams at least not for you.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Comma after 'dreams'. Unless you're going for a sort of mysterious thing where the run on sentences show how unearthly this being is.</p>
<p>Also, odd how its dialogue switches to a different, <strong><em>bolded and italcized style</em></strong> here wheras earlier, <em>it spoke like this</em>.</p>
<p>Also, earlier, it was addressed as <strong>Unknown</strong>, whereas here, there's no addressing as such.</p>
<p>Maybe I'm just a stickler for consistency, I don't know, but I found this a tad jarring.</p>
<blockquote>
<p><strong><em>Wrong</em></strong></p>
</blockquote>
<p>No period.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Rossi: What are you talking about?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I personally imagine this character responding with 'What you do mean 'wrong?'' as a way to sass it. Can't explain why.</p>
<p>I just finished the first Addendum.</p>
<p>Hmmm&#8230;so far, I find the dialogue pretty decent. There's a good sense of mystery and a good sense of buildup, but I don't feel attached to Rossi. She feels like she's just there.</p>
<p>Also, the hooded figure feels a little too 'generic mysterious dream person' to me.</p>
<p>Like, I really dig it all, but it's missing a little bit of that pizzazz which makes me go from nodding my head and approving to making the following face:</p>
<p>:o</p>
<p>And losing all breath at the insane BS occuring before me.</p>
<p>Descriptions are lovely, though and the use of dream logic is very good. A little too downplayed, though, in my opinion; it's a dream and yet, despite lapses in timeline and everything being misty and hard to make out with shadowy figures, it doesn't get weird enough in my opinion. The weirdest we see is the dream figure levitating and twirling in the air. It's a dream and I think the surreal nature can be cranked up a notch or 12.</p>
<p>Then again, I can see that that isn't what you're really going for, so this part can be taken however you wish.</p>
<p>Personally, I just love seeing dream logic become as surreal and weird as possible. Probably just me.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>11. There is no body of water within twenty kilometers of Kayaköy.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I like this touch here to show the difference between the 'real' version and the dream version.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Waltham: I can get to the edge of town, it’s not infinite… but then I’ll blank and it will fold in on itself; fall apart until it reforms and I’m sent right back to the fucking church..</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Lovely dream logic. Sorry I'm being a broken record, I just really love weird things.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Waltham: I’m not alone here. I thought I was, but I’m not. There’s something here. I haven’t seen anything but… I’m being watched.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This feels a tad too rehearsed.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Waltham: I'll be the judge of that. I said, come out where I can see you.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>You are looking right at me. Do you like it?</p>
<p>Needs a space between the two.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The street and buildings are also exhibiting non-Euclidean geometrics as they fold in upon themselves, shifting the camera between different elevations and rapidly restructuring from one layout to another.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This. I personally would like more stuff like this. That said, I'm having a difficult time imagining all of this. Then again, describing non-euclidean geometry is very difficult, so I'm not really sure what else to offer here.</p>
<p>Personally, this makes me think of the video game Control when I imagine the walls moving. Same with the streets.</p>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Do you like it this way?</strong></p>
<p>[Waltham does not respond. She is believed to be unconscious.]</p>
<p><strong>Oh.</strong></p>
</blockquote>
<p>So the thing has a clumsy side. I&#8230;don't really like this scene. To me, this moment feels almost Tom and Jerry-ish in a piece that's meant to feel melancholy and strange.</p>
<blockquote>
<p><strong><em>And there’s no one else… You have to stay!</em></strong></p>
</blockquote>
<p>This was the twist that gave me chills.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>After her debriefing, the current Special Containment Procedures were put in place. To date, no further SCP-XXXX events have occurred.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Well, shit. The hooded figure is just lonely and wants company. Well, that's a twist I wasn't expecting.</p>
<p>Other than that last bit, a good bit of the scenes just felt really rehearsed. The sequence of events were intriguing enough to keep me going and it was built up well and the dialogue was serviceable, but I think I can just summarize it as that:serviceable.</p>
<p>The twist? Fantastic.</p>
<p>I can understand the clumsy moment earlier now. The child-like clinginess and that clumsy moment from earlier, the way it begs for people to stay. It's like a lonely little kid that just wants friends.</p>
<p>That's a great twist.</p>
<p>I just think the journey along the way needs to be patched up.</p>
<p>Rossi and Waltham just feel like vehicles to show some weird stuff happenng.</p>
