<p>Personally, I really like the idea, since the concept of childhood memories being twisted into can be truly terrifying and has a lot of narrative potential. To add to the concept, perhaps the tunnel emits a memetic effect that causes an individual who gets to close to be drawn towards it? Or perhaps they can see or hear a part of their favorite childhood memory just outside the tunnel, causing them to be drawn inside, following it out of curiosity?</p>
<p>(One of my favorite childhood memories is playing outside in the snow on Christmas day at my grandparents house.)</p>

